# Third-party material referenced here

**What is licensed by this repository is Felipe Becerra's own work**: the code,
the reverse-engineering of the QY100's SysEx and pattern formats, and the
written record of how each finding was established. What follows is not, and is
identified here rather than silently folded into the licence.

## Yamaha

`voces.json`, `frases.json`, `estilos.json` and `tambores.json` are tables of
**facts read off Yamaha's own documentation and firmware**: program numbers,
voice and style names, preset-phrase indices, note assignments. They exist so
software can address the device correctly. The names in them are Yamaha's; the
tables are not claimed as original work, and are provided for interoperability.

"Yamaha", "QY100", "QY70" and "XG" are Yamaha Corporation's marks, used here
only to say which device this software talks to. This project is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or supported by Yamaha.

The manuals, the Data Filer application and the firmware image are **not
included** in this repository. Citations throughout are by page number and
resolve against the originals.

## qyTools

`docs/qy100-protocolo.md` cites the protocol datasheet of
[qyTools](https://github.com/Max-Coppola/qyTools) (Max Coppola), which
independently corroborated the event grammar and corrected one hypothesis of
ours. Its author confirmed the citation is fine. **No qyTools code is used
here** — qyTools is AGPLv3, and only its documented findings are referenced,
implemented independently from the described behaviour.

## Reference dumps

The `.syx` files under `qy100-syx/dumps/` are captures of the author's own
device holding his own patterns.

## TRIBE Player

`tambores.json` maps the articulation layout of TRIBE Player 2 (Tribe
Instruments) so that loops played with it can be addressed. It is a note-number
map, not sample content; no audio from that library is included or
redistributed. Using the tools that read it requires owning the plugin.
